  "methodology": [
    "Before: immutable 2c89d41 file-reader services. After: pinned history binary/assets. Same selected files and unchanged original history; twenty sequential raw-body Node fetch probes per project per revision, 100 ms between reads, no browser/profiler/check process during probes. JSON parsing is outside each timed body read. These are small within-run empirical percentiles, not field statistics.",
    "Two sequential actual Chrome captures after deployment: Riemann, then EthLib. Chrome 149, normal motion, 1440x960, no throttling, CDP tracing/CPU sampling, no simultaneous validation job. All seven served JS bundles match the hidden-map build byte-for-byte. No native perf sampler in these captures.",
    "Browser EventDispatch measures synchronous handlers. Input/two-rAF is a scheduling proxy, not physical presentation or INP. Resize can coalesce; p95 of eight/one samples is the maximum. Initial/same-node and alternating-target selections are separate. Target source lines and per-selection camera are retained in raw captures.",
    "Native completed spans overlap. Do not sum nested stages or interpret wall minus thread CPU as I/O wait. Startup/host-refresh history materialization is retained separately from status reads. No history fetch or materialization occurs during gesture phases.",
    "Riemann had nearly empty history and unchanged state bytes/native computation. Its Node response p95 increased from 11.6 to 44.1 ms, while the actual settled browser response p95 is 10.8 ms. Transport/client timing remains an adapter measurement; this record does not claim a universal response-time improvement.",
    "The original history hash sorts JSON object keys while preserving arrays and decoded strings. It is a measurement oracle, not an authority/cache identity. Raw traces contain local source context and remain under target/.",
    "Inference remains unapproved in both actual services. Browser/TUI regression replies are scripted. These checks do not establish live-model quality, cold installation, local inference or confidentiality.",
    "Node transfer probes count decoded arrayBuffer body bytes. Browser traffic retains Playwright-reported responseBodySize separately; these byte boundaries differ slightly and must not be treated as identical payload measurements."
